// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	TS045 VSC90 LampTray and OVD PCB draft 0.7.test
// Project:		VSC90
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    29/07/24
//
//Description: Using the nano inside TE209 to control the relay (x2) for 5V regulator  to the PICKkit4 and the power on button.
// Check current fw and if not expect updates the fw. 
// Steps 3 to 4.6 are setup/logic for the test box itself
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
//DISPLAY: lamptrayPCB1.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the Test box (TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
//DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the Test box (TE209).
b. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: TE209				// Connect to the Nano in the TE209
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 	// TURN Power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 	// TURN Pickit RELAY OFF
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF: 							// True result, current is good
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:


#4.2: Connect to the test box
a. If error message below is diplayed, then click OK to continue. 
.
ERROR on line 71, CONNECT_ VSC90 - Not available.
DELAY: 9000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE PC AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90	 				// Test connection to the FDTI chip
IF_NOT: 						// If wrong FTDI porgram
GOTO: #4.3: 					// Reprogram the FTDI and PIC
GOTO: #4.6: 					// FTDI is correct now check the PIC is programmed correctly 


#4.3: program the FTDI 
EXE: ftdi_programmer_vsc90.exe
#4.3.1: program the PIC
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000
GOTO: #4.4: // 

#4.3.2: program the PIC attempt 2 
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000

#4.4:  Press the I/O Power button and turn on the test box
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 				
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.4: 					// There is fault with the current reading, go back and try again 

#4.5: Connect again
DELAY: 7000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4: 						// GO BACK TO THE START

#4.6: PCB Program version check.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE 			// Check connection to the PIC chip
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
[%TYPE% STR_EQ VSC90] 			// Evaluates the FW by checking inside the [] and set true or false flag
IF:
GOTO: #5: 						// Checks and programming complete goto the start of tests
ELSE: 							// PIC is not programmed correctly still
IMPORTANT: Cannot program the test box (PIC). Please check connections to the PIC Kit and PCB.
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #4.3.2: 					// Try programming the PIC again


#5: Test box f/W  version check
COMMAND: VSC90  LBUILD
READLINE: VSC90  LBUILD
Returned Lamptray FW Version is = %LBUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . No communication to PIC device


#6: PCB communication check
COMMAND: VSC90 ENUM
READLINE: VSC90 ENUM 
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = V90LAMPTRAY,ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ V90LAMPTRAY,ZOOM,EEPROM,]// evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#7: Setup the COAX driver and hall sensor feedback.
a. Connect the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212) to  J8 and J7 on the UUT.
b. Click OK to continue.
IMPORTANT: Ensure that the Brown cable is fitted in the correct orientation.
DISPLAY: Coax.png
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 S?? // check the system is in the correct state before homeing
READLINE: VSC90 Sstatus 
Expected result is = 11
Returned result is = %Sstatus%
RANGE: %Sstatus% 11 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation
COMMAND: VSC90 C4h // home it 
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: VSC90 C4h // home it again for full 360 area
DELAY: 1500

#7.1: Test COAX driver and hall sensor feedback
COMMAND: VSC90 S?? // check the system is in the correct state before homing
READLINE: VSC90 Sstatus 
Expected result is = 3
Returned result is = %Sstatus%
RANGE: %Sstatus% 3 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#7.2: Removed the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212
CLICK_OK:


#8: Check the LSTATUS is zero
COMMAND: VSC90 LSTATUS 
READLINE: VSC90 LSTATUS
RANGE: %LSTATUS% 0 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

 

#9: Left flap setup:
a. Set the switch to the on position 'O'on the Flap Detection Switch (TE160).
b. Connect the Flap Detection Switch (TE160) to the Left Flap connector on the PCB.
c. Set the switch to the on position 'I'.
DISPLAY: FlapSetup1.PNG
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 LSTATUS 
READLINE: VSC90 LSTATUS 
RANGE: %LSTATUS% 2 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10: Right Flap setup
a. Set the switch to the on position 'O'on the Flap Detection Switch (TE160).
b. Connect the Flap Detection Switch (TE160) to the Right Flap connector on the PCB.
c. Set the switch to the on position 'I'.
DISPLAY: FlapSetup2.PNG
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 LSTATUS 
READLINE: VSC90 LSTATUS 
RANGE: %LSTATUS% 4 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#11: Front Flap setup:
a. Set the switch to the on position 'O'on the Flap Detection Switch (TE160).
b. Connect the Flap Detection Switch (TE160) to the Front Flap connector on the PCB.
DISPLAY: FlapSetup3.PNG
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 LSTATUS 
READLINE: VSC90 LSTATUS 
RANGE: %LSTATUS% 16 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#12: Check CPLD and Test the OVD LEDs.
a. Check LED27 on the PCB is flashing to confirm CPLD is programmed.
b. Remove the Flap Detection Switch (TE160) from the UUT.
C. Fit the UUT the PCB Fixture TE217. 
d. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
PASS_FAIL: #12:



